•
Described the number and location of tolling points needed to optimize revenue while
minimizing operational costs and inconvenience to the public;
•
Provided information for developing a strategy to gain federal approval for tolling, obtaining
environmental clearances, and resolving possible legal challenges.
In 2010, the Wyoming Legislature voted against continued development of the tolling concept. Since
then, no further studies regarding the potential for tolling within Wyoming have occurred.
